You can use `Promise.all` to handle a list of API calls and get their results. Here's an example:

```javascript
const apiCalls = [
  fetch('https://api.example.com/data1'),
  fetch('https://api.example.com/data2'),
  fetch('https://api.example.com/data3')
];

Promise.all(apiCalls)
  .then(responses => Promise.all(responses.map(r => r.json())))
  .then(data => {
    console.log(data); // Array of results
  })
  .catch(error => {
    console.error('Error:', error);
  });
```

This code first waits for all API calls to complete, then converts each response to JSON, and finally logs the results.
